        "original_id": "976e8878-d2e7-579e-b284-1203dd4d4b60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Shia LaBeouf, Christopher Beau Landon, D. J. Caruso, Carl Ellsworth, David Morse, Sarah Roemer, Carrie-Anne Moss, Michael Landon\n- Works: Disturbia, Even Stevens, Paranormal Activity films\n- Organizations: Disney Channel\n- Awards: Young Artist Award, Daytime Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Beau Landon was born on February 27, 1975, and he is an American film director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- Shia Saide LaBeouf was born on June 11, 1986, and he is an American actor, performance artist, and filmmaker.\n- Shia LaBeouf received a Young Artist Award nomination in 2001 for playing Louis Stevens in the Disney Channel series Even Stevens.\n- Shia LaBeouf won a Daytime Emmy Award in 2003 for his role as Louis Stevens in Even Stevens.\n- Disturbia is a 2007 American horror thriller film directed by D. J. Caruso and written by Christopher Landon and Carl Ellsworth.\n- Disturbia stars Shia LaBeouf, David Morse, Sarah Roemer, and Carrie-Anne Moss.\n- Christopher Landon is best known as the writer of the 2007 film Disturbia and the last three Paranormal Activity films.\n- Christopher Landon is the son of late actor Michael Landon.",
